xt":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"velocity"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"FIDELITY TODO: the exact default constants (Momentum Friction, Rubber Band Friction, decel rate)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"live as port default ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"values"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" inside origami.DragSettings — reading them needs FlatBuffers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"port-value decoding, which the parser doesn’t do yet. Until then the momentum decay uses the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system’s velocity projection (","type":"text"},{"code":"predictedEndTranslation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and rubber-band uses the iOS-standard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constant (0.55). Mark these for replacement once the parser extracts DragSettings’ real defaults.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami","title":"Swami","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own